      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "model/Predictable CREATE clone addresses bypass _isProtocolDestination before deployment, locking quote payouts and allowing cross-clone prize transfers",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "RaffleFactory.createRaffle deploys clones with Clones.clone(raffleImplementation) (EVM CREATE opcode), making every future clone address deterministic from (address(factory), nonce). Before a future clone R_future is deployed, R_future.code.length == 0 and canonicalFactory.isRaffle(R_future) == false. Consequently, R_future passes RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams and Raffle._isProtocolDestination during Raffle.initialize (as sponsorRecipient) and Raffle._update (as a ticket recipient in buyEntries or transferFrom), and bypasses ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received. Once R_future is deployed by a subsequent createRaffle call, isRaffle[R_future] becomes true and R_future.code.length == 45: (1) Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds calls _transferQuote(R_future, amount), which re-checks _isProtocolDestination and permanently reverts with InvalidQuoteDestination(R_future), locking sponsorProceeds; (2) Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize and Raffle.redeemWinningTicket (in Status.NftWon) omit _isProtocolDestination and call prizeToken.transferFrom(address(this), R_future, prizeTokenId), moving the prize NFT into clone R_future in violation of the cross-clone asset isolation invariant and stranding the NFT permanently; (3) any ticket owned by R_future can never be redeemed or refunded because Raffle has no outbound call to redeemWinningTicket or refundTickets; (4) if protocolTreasury is configured to a future clone CREATE address R_k in the RaffleFactory constructor, createRaffle permanently reverts at raffle k with UnsafeProtocolDestination.\nAssumptions: A caller or sponsor specifies a precomputed future CREATE address of RaffleFactory before that clone index is deployed.; At least one subsequent createRaffle call occurs to deploy the clone at that predicted address."
          },
