        {
          "ruleId": "model/Decoupled sponsorProceeds payout in Status.NftWon allows sponsor to claim 95% of buyer USDC even when prizeToken delivery fails in redeemWinningTicket",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "In Status.NftWon, _settleWinningTicket allocates 95% of unsettledPot to sponsorProceeds and 5% to protocolFees in storage without transferring prizeToken or verifying that prizeToken remains transferable to the winning ticket owner. Raffle.releaseSponsorProceeds only checks sponsorProceeds != 0 and does not require prizeClaimed == true when status == Status.NftWon. If the arbitrary ERC-721 prizeToken is pausable, blacklist-enabled, expiring, soulbound-after-escrow, or sponsor-controlled and reverts (or fails the post-transfer ownerOf check) during redeemWinningTicket, the sponsor still extracts 95% of buyer USDC while the winner cannot receive the NFT and the raffle cannot transition from Status.NftWon to Status.Refunding.\nAssumptions: The escrowed prizeToken is an arbitrary ERC-721 contract that succeeds during createRaffle safeTransferFrom but reverts or blocks transfer when redeemWinningTicket is called after settlement."
