        {
          "ruleId": "model/Discontinuous payout cliff at reserveEntries and unrestricted single-buyer under-target draw enable sponsor self-purchase arbitrage and 20% fee extraction",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "When totalEntries crosses reserveEntries, settlement switches discontinuously from Status.CashWon (80% winnerProceeds, 15% sponsorProceeds, 5% protocolFees, plus prize NFT returned to sponsor) to Status.NftWon (0% winnerProceeds, 95% sponsorProceeds, 5% protocolFees). Because neither sponsor nor sponsorRecipient is blocked in buyEntries, a sponsor receives a 95% rebate on every entry bought once totalEntries >= reserveEntries (paying $0.05 net per $1.00 entry) and can buy the shortfall right before endTime to capture 80% of existing buyers' pot plus proportional probability of winning back the NFT. Conversely, when totalEntries < reserveEntries and only a single buyer (or single ticket) participated, requestDraw can still be called at endTime to force Status.CashWon, extracting 15% sponsorProceeds + 5% protocolFees from the sole buyer while returning the NFT to the sponsor.\nAssumptions: Economic mechanism treats sponsor entries identically to external buyer entries and permits draws when ticketCount == 1 below reserveEntries."
          },
