        {
          "ruleId": "model/Unbounded reserveEntries upper limit, unrestricted secondary ticket transfers during Status.Drawing, and ERC-1167 ReentrancyGuard cold-slot gas overhead",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Three defense-in-depth and gas hygiene issues exist across RaffleFactory and Raffle: (1) RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams only checks reserveEntries != 0 and enforces no upper bound on uint128 reserveEntries, allowing raffles where reserveEntries exceeds total USDC supply so Status.NftWon is unreachable; (2) Raffle._update does not restrict ERC-721 ticket transfers during Status.Drawing or after draw fulfillment, exposing open secondary-market orders or bids on tickets to mempool front-running once the VRF fulfillment transaction is visible; (3) Raffle inherits storage-backed ReentrancyGuard (where _status starts at 0 in uninitialized ERC-1167 clone storage rather than _NOT_ENTERED = 1), charging the first buyEntries caller a 20,000-gas 0-to-1 SSTORE penalty, and hardcodes VRF_CALLBACK_GAS_LIMIT = 300_000 even though fulfillRandomWords only writes 4 storage slots.\nAssumptions: Target EVM is cancun (as configured in foundry.toml), where transient storage (EIP-1153) is available."
          },
